  "titulo": "Passive in compound tenses: ha sido construido",
  "subtitulo": "Los platos han sido lavados. El ganador habrá sido elegido.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "In compound tenses, the passive uses haber + sido + participle: ha sido construido, había sido vendida, habrán sido elegidos. Sido never changes; the main participle agrees with the subject. The agent comes with por.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "haber (any tense)",
            "+ sido",
            "+ participle (agrees)",
            "(+ por + agent)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "tense",
            "example",
            "English"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "present perfect",
              "ha sido lavado",
              "has been washed"
            ],
            [
              "pluperfect",
              "había sido lavado",
              "had been washed"
            ],
            [
              "future perfect",
              "habrá sido lavado",
              "will have been washed"
            ],
            [
              "conditional perfect",
              "habría sido lavado",
              "would have been washed"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Sido** is invariable; the **last** participle agrees: **las manzanas habían sido horneadas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Active → passive: the object becomes the subject: **El chef ha horneado las manzanas** → **Las manzanas han sido horneadas por el chef**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In speech, **se** or impersonal **ellos** is more natural: **ya lavaron los platos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **sido** is a fixed hinge; only the last word moves."
        }
      ]
    },
